{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Minimal Usage
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Minimal Usage}
Include the {\b CARR} header:\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid {\cf21 #include "carray/carr.h"}\par
}
\par
Initialize a vector, add elements, reverse, delete an element, and destroy it:\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid {\cf18 int} a = 10;\par
{\cf18 int} b = 20;\par
\par
CARR vec = carr_init(4, {\cf17 true});\par
\par
carr_pushBack(&vec, &a);\par
carr_pushBack(&vec, &b);\par
carr_pushFront(&vec, &b);\par
\par
carr_replaceIndex(&vec, &a, 1);\par
carr_reverse(&vec);\par
carr_deleteIndex(&vec, 0, {\cf17 true});\par
\par
carr_destroy(&vec);\par
}
\par
Check returned {\f2 {\b CARRError}}  values to handle operation failures.\par}
